  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\n## What changed\n\nK5 of the path kernel (#4023): the entry and exit stage, in `crates/pathkernel/src/entry/` (the record's folder: `air`, `hole`, `column`, `material`, `exit`, with `proof`, `room` and `stage`). `entry.rs` moves to `entry/proof.rs`. No old planner calls the stage. With the default planner switch, the output does not change.\n\n- `EntryStage` tries the entries in the record's order. The asked entry outside material comes first. Then: an arc lead from the air outside the stock (#3746), a pre-drilled hole, a cleared column. A helix or a ramp into material is used only when the user selected an entry into material. A plunge is used only when asked and when the tool can plunge.\n- When no entry fits, the stage refuses by name: `NO_SAFE_ENTRY` or `NO_MATERIAL_ENTRY`, at the cut start, with a fix text.\n- `EntryPlanner::entry` now returns `Result<Verdict<Entry>, Refusal>`. An entry of another kind than asked carries a named `Fallback` (law 4). `named()` builds the verdict. `needs_fallback()` is the one rule.\n- `Entry::led` is the single gate. It keeps the descent check of the skeleton and binds a new `Lead` (the moves in the plane onto the cut) to its room.\n- The exit: `Exit::proved` checks that the lead-out starts at the end of the last cut and that the retract is at or above the material top. The lead-out goes only where the tool cuts nothing (cleared material, the band of the last cut, the air). Else the tool goes straight up. `Exit::new` now refuses an unproved lead-out.\n- For Outside, the air entry keeps the tool radius from a keep-out (a clamp at the stock edge).\n- `camcraft-geometry`: `geo2d::arc_points` (an arc as chords within a tolerance) and `Region::holds_path` (no stretch of a polyline outside a region), with unit tests.\n\n## Public surface (`camcraft_pathkernel::entry`)\n\n- `trait EntryPlanner { fn entry(..) -> Result<Verdict<Entry>, Refusal>; fn exit(..) -> Result<Exit, Refusal> }`\n- `EntryStage::new(Heights, ArcChoice, chord_tol)`, `Heights::new(top, clear, retract)`, `ArcChoice::new(radius, sweep_deg)`\n- `EntryChoice::with_material(MaterialChoice)`, `MaterialChoice::new(angle_deg, helix_radius)`, `DEFAULT_DESCENT_ANGLE`\n- `EntryKind::name()`, `EntryKind::into_material()`, `needs_fallback(asked, used)`, `named(entry, choice, why, notes)`\n- `Lead::new(pts, room)`, `Entry::led(..)`, `Entry::lead()`\n- `Exit::proved(last, lead_out, retract, top)`\n- Refusal reasons: `NO_SAFE_ENTRY`, `NO_MATERIAL_ENTRY`, `NOT_PLANAR`, `NO_DIRECTION`, `ENTRY_GEOMETRY`, `BAD_HEIGHTS`, `BAD_ARC`, `BAD_MATERIAL_CHOICE`, `LEAD_SHORT`, `LEAD_NOT_FLAT`, `LEAD_OFF_ROOM`, `LEAD_GAP`, `EXIT_OFF_CUT`, `RAPID_IN_MATERIAL`, `UNPROVED_LEAD_OUT`; `ROOM_TOL`\n- `camcraft_geometry::geo2d::{arc_points, MAX_ARC_CHORDS}`, `Region::holds_path`\n\n## Pins (`camcraft-pathkernel`, binary `laws`)\n\n- `entry_stage::a_closed_pocket_with_no_hole_and_no_helix_or_ramp_is_refused_by_name` (also with a tool that can plunge: no plunge without the user's choice)\n- `entry_stage::an_open_pocket_enters_in_air_with_an_arc_lead`\n- `entry_stage::an_air_entry_at_the_stock_edge_keeps_off_a_clamp`\n- `entry_stage::an_asked_helix_enters_the_closed_pocket_in_the_centre_area`\n- `entry_stage::an_asked_helix_that_does_not_fit_falls_back_to_a_named_ramp` (and a refusal when the ramp does not fit either: never a plunge)\n- `entry_stage::a_plunge_needs_the_users_choice_and_a_plunging_tool`\n- `entry_stage::a_predrilled_hole_serves_the_closed_pocket`, `entry_stage::a_cleared_column_serves_the_closed_pocket`\n- `exit::the_exit_leads_out_into_the_air_then_retracts`, `exit::the_exit_of_a_ring_in_uncut_material_goes_straight_up`, `exit::an_exit_is_refused_off_its_cut_or_below_the_top`\n- `exit::a_lead_stays_flat_and_in_its_room_and_starts_where_the_descent_ends`, `exit::a_fallback_is_named_for_another_kind_than_asked`, `exit::the_stage_choices_refuse_bad_values_by_name`\n- `l4_fallback::the_entry_stage_passes_l4_and_l5`, `l4_fallback::l4_holds_for_a_named_entry_fallback`\n- A proof for another place: the existing `entry::a_descent_outside_the_proved_area_is_refused_for_each_area_proof` and `entry::a_predrilled_entry_stays_in_a_known_hole` stay green on `Entry::led`.\n- `camcraft-geometry` lib: `geo2d::arc::tests::*` (4 tests).\n\n## The law suite (#4175)\n\n#4175 merged to the side branch before this PR. This PR changes it to the new signature:\n- the stand-ins return `Ok(Verdict::done(entry))` (`standins.rs`, `l5_entry.rs`, `l4_fallback.rs`);\n- `kit::Run` gets `entries: Vec<Verdict<Entry>>`; `kit::run` takes the entry out of its verdict;\n- `check_l4` counts an entry as silent when `needs_fallback(asked, used)` is true and the verdict has no fallback of `Stage::Entry`. Before, it treated `ArcLead` as an entry into material.\n\n## Decisions\n\n`docs/decisions/4178-kernel-entry-exit.md` (11 items). The main ones:\n- the trait returns a `Verdict`, as the guide and the load stages do;\n- the legal room of the tool centre is read from the K1 region (centre, air, the band outside each stock edge loop, less the keep-out);\n- K1's air band is one tool radius wide, so the approach distance is limited to half the tool radius, with a status line note;\n- one descent angle for the helix and the ramp (default 3 degrees), the helix radius at most the tool radius (default half);\n- a hole narrower than the tool serves only a tool that can plunge.\n\n## Gates (final tree)\n\nThe diff touches `camcraft-geometry`, so the quick gate falls back to batch.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/4025-kernel-region` on `0daa62a0e`: 1223 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (60.5 min, 6 jobs, under xvfb). It includes `clippy -D warnings` (all crates but kernel), `pathkernel suites: laws`, `geometry suites: lib`, and `example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work` (all ok).\n- `cargo xtask gate light --base origin/issue/4025-kernel-region`: 7 steps, 0 failed.\n- K1 (#4181) merged while the gate ran. The merge of `origin/side/path-kernel` (`cc00b664f`) changes no file (`git diff HEAD^1 HEAD` is empty), so the gated tree is the tree of this head.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No kind calls the stage yet: no posted program, no CL law reading (#4154) of a kernel entry.\n- The arc leads are chord points; the exact circle (G2/G3) is not recorded.\n- A part that touches the stock edge (its loop is a part wall, so the band outside it is not legal room): reasoned, not pinned.\n- An Inside pocket that runs off the stock enters in air only when the caller gives the outside area as `cleared`: no pin.\n- `Proof` is not `#[non_exhaustive]`: a later proof kind is a breaking change of the enum. `EntryKind`, `Step` and `KernelRegion` stay open.\n\nEffort: max\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #4178\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
